1845       title 'Logistic Regression Random-Effects Model';
1846       data seeds;
1847       input r n seed extract @@;
1848       ind = _N_;
1849       datalines;

NOTE: SAS went to a new line when INPUT statement reached past the end of a line.
NOTE: The data set WORK.SEEDS has 21 observations and 5 variables.

1856       ;
1857       proc mcmc data=seeds outpost=postout seed=332786 nmc=1000 nbi=200;
1858       ods select PostSumInt;
1859       parms beta0 0 beta1 0 beta2 0 beta3 0 s2 1;
1860       prior s2 ~ igamma(0.01, s=0.01);
1861       prior beta: ~ general(0);
1862       w = beta0 + beta1*seed + beta2*extract + beta3*seed*extract;
1863       random delta ~ normal(w, var=s2) subject=ind;
1864       pi = logistic(delta);
1865       model r ~ binomial(n = n, p = pi);
1866       run;

NOTE: Tuning the proposal distribution.
NOTE: Generating the burn-in samples.
NOTE: Beginning sample generation.
NOTE: The data set WORK.POSTOUT has 1000 observations and 31 variables.
